-30 21:02:40.646 xcodebuild[56259:34475551]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-09-30 21:02:40.961 xcodebuild[56259:34475550] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n+ vm-continuation-invoke\n     1\t(ns yin.vm.module\n     2\t  \"Module system for Yin VM v2.\n     3\t\n     4\t   The v1 module system kept two `defonce` atoms and mutated them at load\n     5\t   time. A registry is a value here: an ordinary map carried in VM state and\n     6\t   supplied by the composition that wires the VM.\n     7\t\n     8\t     (-> (empty-registry)\n     9\t         (register-host-module 'my.lib {'foo (fn [x] x)} profiles)\n    10\t         (register-stream-module))\n    11\t\n    12\t   Nothing in this namespace runs at load time, and nothing registers itself.\n    13\t   A composition that wants Yin source to reach `(stream/...)` registers the\n    14\t   stream module explicitly and supplies `:make-stream` beside it.\"\n    15\t  (:require\n    16\t    [clojure.string :as str]\n    17\t    [dao.jing :as jing]\n    18\t    [dao.stream :as stream]\n    19\t    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n    20\t\n    21\t\n    22\t;; =============================================================================\n    23\t;; Registry values\n    24\t;; =============================================================================\n    25\t\n    26\t(defn empty-registry\n    27\t  \"An empty module registry value.\"\n    28\t  []\n    29\t  {:modules {}, :effect-handlers {}})\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\t(defn- symbol->path\n    33\t  \"Split a dotted symbol into a get-in path of symbols.\n    34\t   'yin.io.file-input-stream → ['yin 'io 'file-input-stream]\"\n    35\t  [sym]\n    36\t  (mapv symbol (str/split (str sym) #\"\\.\")))\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t(defn- walk-path\n    40\t  \"Descend a registry's :modules map along path, a sequence of symbols.\n    41\t\n    42\t   Namespace segments step through plain maps until the path reaches a\n    43\t   module entry (a map carrying :manifest); the remaining segments read\n    44\t   that entry's task-local lowered `:bindings` when it holds them -- a\n    45\t   linked module (yin.vm.linker.md section 8.3) -- and its `:slice`\n    46\t   otherwise, which for a host module is the host values themselves, so\n    47\t   a binding name resolves to its export.\"\n    48\t  [node path]\n    49\t  (if (seq path)\n    50\t    (if (and (map? node) (contains? node :manifest))\n    51\t      (get-in node (into [(if (contains? node :bindings) :bindings :slice)]\n    52\t                         path))\n    53\t      (when-let [child (get node (first path))]\n    54\t        (walk-path child (rest path))))\n    55\t    node))\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\t(defn module-entry\n    59\t  \"The registry entry of module `module-name` in `modules` (a registry's\n    60\t   `:modules` map), or nil when the dotted path reaches no module entry.\"\n    61\t  [modules module-name]\n    62\t  (let [node (reduce (fn [node seg] (when (map? node) (get node seg)))\n    63\t                     modules\n    64\t                     (symbol->path module-name))]\n    65\t    (when (and (map? node) (contains? node :manifest)) node)))\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\t(defn assoc-module\n    69\t  \"Return registry with `entry` installed as module `module-name`.\"\n    70\t  [registry module-name entry]\n    71\t  (assoc-in (or registry (empty-registry))\n    72\t            (into [:modules] (symbol->path module-name))\n    73\t            entry))\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\t(defn link-module\n    77\t  \"The `linked` transition's registry update (yin.vm.linker.md sections\n    78\t   7.3 and 8.3): `registry` gains the module `manifest` names as the\n    79\t   portable encoding of acts 1 to 3 -- `{:manifest m :address a\n    80\t   :derivation d :slice {sym encoded} :stores {address snapshot} :cells\n    81\t   {cell-id cell} :images {identity image}}` -- never lowered values. `a`\n    82\t   is the manifest's own address; `lifted` is the act-1 lift, `{:slice\n    83\t   :stores :cells :images}`, the cells being the logical cursor cells its\n    84\t   references name (r9) and the images the verified origin images a\n    85\t   receiving task attaches.\n    86\t   Each receiving task lowers the entry into its own `:bindings`.\"\n    87\t  [registry manifest derivation lifted]\n    88\t  (assoc-module registry\n    89\t                (:yin.module/name manifest)\n    90\t                {:manifest manifest,\n    91\t                 :address (jing/segment-key manifest),\n    92\t                 :derivation derivation,\n    93\t                 :slice (:slice lifted),\n    94\t                 :stores (:stores lifted),\n    95\t                 :cells (:cells lifted),\n    96\t                 :images (:images lifted)}))\n    97\t\n    98\t\n    99\t(defn module-entries\n   100\t  \"Every `[name entry]` a registry value holds, the module name read back\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
